{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011ChLe9wB1FGnugnUWvND9e","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"`RidgeClassifierCV` now accepts `store_cv_values`. Before, the documentation described the flag but the constructor rejected it with the `TypeError` from the issue.\n\nThe fix is in `sklearn/linear_model/ridge.py`:\n- **Constructor:** `RidgeClassifierCV.__init__` takes `store_cv_values=False` and hands it to the base class it inherits from. That base class already stores `cv_values_` and raises a `ValueError` if the flag is combined with `cv != None`.\n- **Docstring:** I added an entry for `store_cv_values` to the parameter list. I also corrected the documented shape of `cv_values_` to `[n_samples, n_targets, n_alphas]`. The classifier always returns a 3-D array, even for two classes.\n\n**Checks:**\n- I ran an example with `store_cv_values=True`. It gives `cv_values_` shape `(100, 3, 3)` for 3 classes and `(100, 1, 3)` for 2 classes, with 3 alphas in both cases.\n- The existing tests in `sklearn/linear_model/tests/test_ridge.py` all pass (35 tests).\n\nI didn't add a new test because the task rules forbid editing test files."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1832,"cache_read_input_tokens":21490,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1832},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d88ded08-6c3b-4ec9-8b85-39586dcf01ff","uuid":"94b341d2-604c-4ff5-84d5-9310b8be9047","timestamp":"2026-11-23T22:22:56.540Z","request_id":"req_011ChLe9vcmykiCgeKQSEPhd"}
